    "node-5e1him": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims RHOB receives air via header H-R and that P-U/P-R monitor it with alarm AL-44. Evidence (IA-D01) confirms the directory states 'RHOB is a local area name' and lists 'Receiving header H-R and indication P-R | RHOB operations'. However, IA-P02 explicitly maps AL-44 to 'RHOB PLC low-pressure input from P-R', but does not confirm that this alarm covers all locations or valve states. The node's detail implies a continuous monitoring capability ('Normal operation involves pressure monitoring...') which is contradicted by the evidence stating data is sampled, not continuous (IA-P01). Furthermore, IA-D01 explicitly disclaims establishing 'pressure available at any given time'.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record confirming that P-R and AL-44 provide sufficient coverage for normal operation monitoring of H-R pressure in the RHOB area.",
      "question": "Does a current piping diagram or operating procedure confirm that header H-R supplies instrument air to the entire RHOB process area, and does alarm AL-44 cover all relevant low-pressure conditions?"
    },
    "node-1rdlpcn": {
      "supported": true,
